    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the repo, and both of its cases pass along with a successful build.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `ownerSegment` field on the owner API. Three coordinated changes, following the project's existing derived-getter + OpenAPI-generated-DTO conventions:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `getOwnerSegment()` derived getter next to the related `getMembershipLevel()`/`getLocality()`/`getTimezone()` getters:\n   ```java\n   public String getOwnerSegment() {\n       String tier = getMembershipLevel() >= 3 ? \"PREMIUM\" : \"STANDARD\";\n       String area = REGION_TIMEZONE.containsKey(getLocality()) ? \"METRO\" : \"REGIONAL\";\n       return tier + \"_\" + area;\n   }\n   ```\n   It reuses `getMembershipLevel()` (TIER = `PREMIUM` at level \u2265 3, else `STANDARD`) and `getLocality()` checked against the existing region map whose keys are exactly NSW/VIC/QLD (AREA = `METRO` for a known region, else `REGIONAL`).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` property (string, `readOnly`, enum of the four valid values) to the `Owner` schema's derived-properties block, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n3. **No mapper change needed** \u2014 `OwnerMapper` auto-maps `ownerSegment` by name (MapStruct converts the `String` from the entity to the generated enum).\n\nThe two acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known NSW city, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city) now pass.",
